</notes>
<segment>
<source>Remove App: Delete all labels for the selected application</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6a06c89e-7cca-45aa-96bd-db7dcb226555">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 85</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Remove All: Delete all custom labels</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="0ac3f192-e072-43ee-852f-2ebd1a2835b1">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 87</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>In addition to that, there is a setting that allows you to use the description of a control as the label of that control if the control has no label. But note: if a custom label has been set, that custom label will overwrite the description, even the original label on the control.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="be07fd8a-5c03-4294-88d1-dc016ee7b25d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 89</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Storage</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="846f0456-ca13-459c-88c5-099c1a040fa0">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 91</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Labels are stored in JSON files in NVDA's configuration directory under a `customLabels` folder. Each application has its own JSON file, making it easy to backup or share labels for specific applications.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="7d5b1248-dcfb-4c57-b909-50ded03f0ec6">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 93</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Known Limitations</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="f6125de3-8a7f-41a8-b1d4-5fc1ce8585a4">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 95</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Web-based applications — Electron and WebView2 apps (such as the new Outlook, Microsoft Teams, Slack, WhatsApp, and Discord): custom labels are now applied in browse mode as well as focus mode. To set or remove a label you must still press NVDA+Space to switch to focus mode first. Regular browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, etc.) are not supported.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="716b92d2-5e91-4930-a9a9-a3bcc3171dba">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 96</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Browse mode — label re-announcement: in browse mode on Electron and WebView2 apps, the full label is announced on every arrow key press on a labelled control. Character-by-character reading of the label is not possible. This is a fundamental limitation of how NVDA constructs the virtual buffer internally and cannot be addressed by the add-on alone.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="4e654f4b-41c4-411a-82b3-3ae825082d36">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 97</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Controls with identical properties: If an application has multiple controls of the same type with the same name (or no name), sometimes custom labels cannot distinguish between them. Labelling one will label all matching controls. This is rare in practice, as most applications assign unique identifiers to their controls.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
